# Architecture

Crestic is a Go CLI wrapper around restic. Config is YAML; pipelines contain jobs (backup, copy).

## Layers

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| CLI | `cmd/` | cobra commands, wiring, flags |
| Use cases | `internal/cases/{feature}/` | `Handler` + `Command` |
| Middleware | `internal/cases/handler/` + `internal/pkg/mw/` | command: `Chain`, `WithLock`, `WithPanicRecovery`; execution: `mw.Chain` |
| Domain | `internal/entity/` | business entities (Job, Pipeline, Config) |
| DTO | `internal/dto/` | YAML config to entity mapping |
| Infra | `internal/engine/{restic,shell,healthchecks,hooks,cron,jobs,pipelines}/` | external services and runners |
| Helpers | `internal/pkg/{mw,paths,panix,testutils}/` | shared utilities |


## Patterns

- New command: `cmd/{cmd}.go` -> handler in `internal/cases/` -> entity/dto as needed
- Handler chain: `handler.Chain(base, WithPanicRecovery, WithLock)` — see `cmd/cron.go` (generic chain in `pkg/mw`)
- Job interface (`internal/entity/job.go`): all job types implement `GetName()`, `GetPipeline()`, `GetFullName()`, `GetHooks()`
- Batch errors: collect and return with `errors.Join()` — see `internal/engine/pipelines/runner.go`

## Layer boundaries

- CLI must not contain business logic
- `entity` must not know about YAML or cobra
- `dto` maps config to entity; handlers work with entity types only
